# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This repository is PUBLIC (DECISIONS.md #17). Zero secrets in git, ever.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Dependencies
node_modules/

# Build output
site/dist/
site/.astro/
lambda/build/
lambda/*.zip

# Terraform
**/.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfplan
crash.log
crash.*.log
terraform.tfvars
*.auto.tfvars
.terraformrc
terraform.rc

# Secrets / credentials
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
.aws/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DECISIONS.md #41 / #44 — the source photograph for the ASCII portrait never
# enters this public repo. Only the generated .txt is committed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
scripts/portrait/source/
scripts/portrait/*.jpg
scripts/portrait/*.jpeg
scripts/portrait/*.png
scripts/portrait/*.webp

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DECISIONS.md #18 / #35 / #41(b) — the capstone originals never enter this
# public repo either. They carry a classmate's face and whatever the camera
# wrote into the file. Only the redacted, metadata-stripped copies produced by
# scripts/capstone/redact.mjs are committed, and blurring is not reversible
# once the original is the only thing that was ever published.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
scripts/capstone/source/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PDFs are a secret-scanning blind spot. Gitleaks reads bytes, and PDF text
# lives in compressed streams, so a phone number inside a PDF passes the scanner
# untouched — the `ph-mobile-number` rule cannot see it.
#
# This is not theoretical: on 2026-08-30 a working résumé containing the phone
# number was staged and committed, and was caught by eye rather than by the
# gate. The compensating control is that no PDF can be committed at all except
# the single sanitized web variant, which is reviewed by hand before it ships.
#
# DECISIONS.md #37.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.pdf
!site/public/resume.pdf

# Raw planning transcripts. These are unedited conversations containing personal
# details (phone number, home address). One was committed in 0314ec4, reached
# GitHub, and had to be scrubbed from history — the exact thing the Gitleaks
# rule in DECISIONS.md #37 exists to prevent. DECISIONS.md is the curated,
# publishable record; the transcripts stay local.
docs/grilling-transcript-*.md
docs/*-transcript-*.md

# Raw camera formats carry full EXIF (GPS, timestamp, device). Never wanted
# anywhere in this repo — see DECISIONS.md #41(b).
*.heic
*.HEIC
*.heif
*.CR2
*.NEF
*.ARW
*.dng
*.DNG

# Un-sanitized capstone install photos. Sanitized copies land in
# site/public/img/ only after EXIF stripping (CI gate, M4).
scripts/photos/original/

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# Build artifact: regenerated by `npm run build` from profile.ts and posts.ts
# (scripts/corpus/build.mjs). Committing it would create a second copy of the
# data that can silently disagree with the first. DECISIONS.md #29.
site/public/corpus.json

# Terraform builds this placeholder zip to create the chat function with; the
# real code is deployed by lambda.yml. Regenerated on every plan.
infra/modules/chatbot/build/
